  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 208 PM EDT Sun Jun 21 2026\n\n- Rain chances this afternoon and overnight\n\nBeneficial light rain for some with no significant impacts \nexpected this afternoon and overnight. Focus for rain is near and\nsouth of I-96 with better chances for more rain the further south\nyou go. \n\nCurrent ensemble probabilities for near I-94 show around 75% chance \nfor one-quarter inch or more, 50% chance for one-half inch or more \nof rain by tomorrow and around a 10% chance of one inch or more. Up \naround I-96 those probabilities drop to around 35% chance for one-\nquarter inch or more, around 15% chance for one-half inch or more \nand near zero percent chance of one inch or more. Up around US-10, \nthe probabilities for one-tenth of an inch or more and one-\nquarter inch or more are both near 0%. \n\nSo most likely case is around a quarter-inch or less near I-96 and a \nhalf-inch or so near/south of I-94. Again...no significant impacts \nexpected from this rain.  \n\nSome lightning may be possible...though chances for that should be \nbetter closer to and south of the Indiana border than up in lower \nMichigan.  \n\n- Cooler than normal temperatures persist through the week \n\nNo change to the overall pattern expected this week with \ntemperatures generally hovering in the mid 70s for highs and in the \n50s for lows. We could see some warming to more summer like \ntemperatures next weekend into the last few days of June with models \nindicating warming temps potentially through the 4th of July \nweekend.",
